PJA 0.0.1 (tag v0.0.1, commit 0776d32, 2026-10-23), https://github.com/YadeWira/PJA,
from the vendor tarball pja-0.0.1-zpaqstd.tar.gz (sha256
d5abf9f6611a9d8137c2fe263a78379ff21266a1b05618f808cc8a789e05dd8d), copied unmodified:
the sources of its zpaq-std plugin, LICENSE (MIT), NOTICE (IJG for the arithmetic-coded
JPEG, CharLS's BSD 3-Clause for JPEG-LS) and VENDOR.md (what it is and how it builds).

zpaq-std's codecs for specific formats, -sa: pja (JPEG) and pjals (JPEG-LS), stream
version 5, full model. Free Pascal: by the project's rule, a codec in Rust or Free
Pascal is built only as a plugin (codecs/pja.dll or pja.so, in the extra-codecs
download), never linked into zpaq-std itself. Every block carries the codec's ZPAQL
decoder (pas/plugin/pjazpaql.inc, pjalszpaql.inc), so any zpaq extracts it without
the plugin; those two programs are frozen under these codec names.
Do not patch these files here: send changes to the PJA repository.
